-- title:
--   Unramified splitting of level 2-cocycles over a p-adic field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and write $\Omega =$ `PadicAlgCl q` for the chosen algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$. Let $K \subseteq \Omega$ be an intermediate field of $\Omega/\mathbb{Q}_q$ that is finite over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, and let $r$ be a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/K) = \Omega \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} \Omega$ to $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, where $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Two compatibility hypotheses are imposed on $r$: for every intermediate field $E$ of $\Omega/K$ finite over $K$ there is an intermediate field $F$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}$ with $r^{-1}(\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/F)) \subseteq \mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/E)$ (`hlevel`), and conversely for every such $F$ there is such an $E$ with $\mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/E) \subseteq r^{-1}(\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/F))$ (`hopen`), both formulated through `fixingSubgroup`. Finally let $c$ be a function on $\mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/K) \times \mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/K)$ with values in the coefficient module `Rep.ofAlgebraAutOnUnits K (PadicAlgCl q)`, assumed to lie in `levelCocycles₂ r` for that module. The conclusion asserts the existence of an integer $N > 0$ such that, with $L = K(\{\zeta \in \Omega : \zeta^{q^N-1} = 1\})$ the intermediate field of $\Omega/K$ generated by the $(q^N-1)$-st roots of unity, the restriction of $c$ along the canonical monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/L) \to \mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/K)$ (the inverse of `IntermediateField.fixingSubgroupEquiv` followed by the inclusion of the fixing subgroup of $L$) lies in `levelCoboundaries₂` for the level map $r$ composed with that same homomorphism and for the coefficient module `Rep.ofAlgebraAutOnUnits L (PadicAlgCl q)`.
--
--   This is the cochain form of the statement that a Brauer class of a $p$-adic field is split by an unramified extension: every continuous $2$-cocycle of $\mathrm{Gal}(\Omega/K)$ with values in $\Omega^\times$ becomes a coboundary after restriction to the Galois group of the unramified layer $K(\mu_{q^N-1})$ for some $N \ge 1$. It is deduced from the corresponding splitting statement at the level of classes, [`groupCohomology.exists_mem_split_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_of_padic`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_mem_split_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_of_padic), and is used in the variant for the Kummer representation, [`groupCohomology.exists_restrict_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_mem_levelCoboundaries2_kummerRep_of_padic`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_restrict_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_mem_levelCoboundaries2_kummerRep_of_padic).
